## Caveats

- The 96 stocks were chosen in 2026 with hindsight bias, and the improved model could
not address the problem. To address the bias, we need the stocks that were actually in the index on each date, including ones later dropped or delisted, plus their prices. Yet, the Yahoo Finance API doesn't have delisted prices. 
- Six models were tried on the same 34 months, so the best t-statistic among them (2.1) is weaker evidence than it looks.
- Prices only: no earnings, valuations or analyst forecasts.

## Takeaway
To conclude, in terms of investment performance, the improved model beats the class model and SPY on return (+150% against +109% and +66%). However, it does not have a better predictive performance, as its rank IC is 0.024 with t = 0.7, compared with rank IC of 0.045 and 
t= 2.1 for the class model. Matter of fact, neither of the two models ranks stocks
reliably since both have rank IC that are not apart from 0 over 34 months. 

Moreover, the Sharpe ratio of the improved model is 1.06, which is also below the 
class model's 1.21. The reason why the 
improved model, despite having lower predictive performance, has higher return
is that it's making a momentum bet on the stocks. The momentum rule returned +142% with a Sharpe ratio of 1.08, and its daily returns in excess of the 96 stocks have a 0.82 correlation with the improved model's. Another reason is that the improved model increases its risk exposure, 
as buying SPY with borrowed money at the same 1.6× beta made +105%.

## Data and code

- Stock prices: daily prices for 96 large U.S. stocks and the S&P 500 ETF (`SPY`), adjusted for splits and dividends, from Yahoo Finance; 4 January 2010 to 12 November 2026 (accessed 13 November 2026). The stock list is the one in the class script.
- Risk-free rate: 13-week Treasury-bill yield (`^IRX`), from Yahoo Finance, same dates.
- Class experiment: final portfolio values of 45 teams, AEDS 6400, Fall 2026, from the instructor's results file.
- Class model: the course's XGBoost script (Yisroel Cahn).

Code, data and every number quoted above: [github.com/1iiiiii/Stock-Return-Boosting](https://github.com/1iiiiii/Stock-Return-Boosting).